DynamoDB:
    DynamoDB > Table > Create Table
    Fill table name (my_DynamoDB) and partition key (User_ID)
    Crate table
    Click in the table and turn on "Deletion protection"

CognitoDB:
    Amazon Cognito > User pools > Create user pool
        Application type > Single-page application (SPA)
        Name your application > my_SPA_app
        Options for sign-in identifiers > Email
        Self-registration > DISABLE!
        Create user directory
        Optional: Amazon Cognito > User pools > Click on [your pool] > Rename > my_user_pool
        Optional: Amazon Cognito > User pools > my_user_pool > Authentication methods > Edit > (Soften the requirements)

    Amazon Cognito > User pools > my_user_pool > Users > Create user
        Invitation message > Send an email invitation
        Email address > [User's email]
        Temporary password > Generate a password
        Create User
    Removal: Amazon Cognito > User pools > my_user_pool > Users > (Select user) > Delete user

    Amazon Cognito > Identity pools > Create identity pool
        User access > Authenticated access
            Authenticated identity sources > Amazon Cognito user pool
        Click "Next"
            IAM role > Create new IAM role
            IAM role name > user_s_IAM_role
        Click "Next"
            User pool ID > my_user_pool
            App client ID > my_SPA_app
        Click "Next"
            Identity pool name > my_identity_pool
        Click "Next"
        Click "Create identity pool"

